  "summary": "Penang betta is a wild mouthbrooding fighting fish native to Peninsular Malaysia and neighbouring areas. The male carries developing eggs and fry in its mouth. On Penang it has been collected in clear hill streams, particularly in sheltered margins with roots and leaf litter.",
